  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>CsCl</mi></math>&nbsp;has body centered type structure in which <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Cs</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></math> occupies at corner of a cube and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Cl</mi><mo>&#8211;</mo></msup></math> occupies the centre of the cube.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><msup><mi>Cs</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><msup><mi>Cl</mi><mo>-</mo></msup></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></math>&nbsp;(where a is the edge length of&nbsp;the cube)</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><msup><mi>Cs</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mi>Cr</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></math></p>"
